words:'knit weave stitch thread scissors leather strip knot fold',pages:[
['Eva introduced Jun to her grandmother, who used to repair the market workers’ uniforms. The old woman could knit a scarf, weave a basket, and stitch a torn pocket. She kept a pair of scissors beside a box of thread and strips of leather.','Eva 介紹 Jun 認識自己的祖母；老奶奶以前替夜市員工修制服。她會編織圍巾、編籃子，也會縫補破掉的口袋。她把剪刀放在線盒和皮革條旁。'],
['From a shelf she took a folded apron. The fabric had a knot at one corner, and a recipe was stitched into its lining. “Your founder could not afford a printed menu,” she said. “So I helped her hide the first one where it would not be lost.”','她從架上拿出一件摺好的圍裙，一角打了個結，食譜縫在內襯裡。「你們的創辦人當年印不起菜單，」她說。「所以我幫她把第一份縫進不會弄丟的地方。」'],
['Jun unfolded the cloth carefully. The recipe listed ordinary, inexpensive food. It had survived because someone repaired it each time the stitches loosened. The secret was less about a perfect dish than about people who refused to abandon one another.','Jun 小心展開布料。食譜列著普通、便宜的食物。它能保存下來，是因為每次縫線鬆脫時都有人修補。秘密與其說是完美料理，不如說是人們不願放棄彼此。']],
quiz:[['Where was the original recipe hidden?','In an apron lining','In a bank','In a mountain cave','Inside a violin','最初的食譜被縫進圍裙內襯。'],['Why did the founder not print the menu?','She could not afford printing','She had forgotten English','She disliked customers','She sold the kitchen','創辦人當年負擔不起印刷。'],['How did the recipe survive?','People kept repairing the stitching','It was copied onto a computer','A magician made it vanish','It was hidden at sea','有人持續修補縫線才保留下食譜。']]
