words:'advertise adviser assist product producer pitch expectation charm exchange',pages:[
['A food producer offered to advertise the market’s new meal. Its adviser said a colorful package could make the product easier to sell. Jun listened politely, but the company’s pitch promised a “secret luxury recipe” that the market did not actually use.','一家食品製造商願意替夜市新餐點打廣告。顧問說，色彩鮮明的包裝可能讓產品更好賣。Jun 禮貌聽著，但公司的推銷說詞承諾「祕密奢華食譜」，市場其實沒有使用那種食譜。'],
['“We need help, but we cannot exchange an honest story for a prettier lie,” Jun said. He asked the producer to assist with ingredients instead. The adviser explained that the sponsor’s expectation was wider sales. Jun replied that the market’s charm came from serving food people could afford.','「我們需要幫忙，但不能用真實故事換一個更漂亮的謊言，」Jun 說。他請製造商改為協助提供食材。顧問說明贊助商期待擴大銷售。Jun 回答，夜市的魅力在於提供人們負擔得起的食物。'],
['They agreed to publish a clear menu with prices and ingredients. The sponsor could appear on the sign without claiming that the meal was something it was not. Jun had finally found a way to honor the old recipe without hiding behind it.','他們同意公布清楚列出價格與食材的菜單。贊助商可以出現在招牌上，但不能把餐點說成它原本不是的樣子。Jun 終於找到尊重舊食譜、又不躲在傳統背後的方法。']],
